# Cloud Functions

- `firebase-functions` v2 APIs: `onCall`, `onSchedule`, `onDocumentUpdated`. Admin SDK modular imports (`firebase-admin/firestore`).
- ESLint google style: double quotes, 2-space indent, max line length 100, JSDoc on exported functions.
- Admin callables:
  ```ts
  const adminUid = assertAdmin(request);
  const input = parseMyInput(request.data);   // pure, from <name>.logic.ts
  const batch = db().batch();
  // ... writes ...
  await batch.commit();
  await writeAuditLog({action: "crossword.saveQuestion", adminUid, targetId: input.id});
  ```
- Player callables: require `request.auth`; check the user is not blocked (`users/{uid}.blockedAt`); idempotent; validate every input; return plain JSON.
- Throw `HttpsError(code, message)` with messages an admin can act on. Validators collect all problems before throwing.
- Pure logic (validation, scoring, encoding) in separate files with `*.test.ts` beside them. No Firestore in pure files.
- New crossword code in `functions/src/crossword/`; export from `functions/src/index.ts`. Region `asia-south1` (set once with `setGlobalOptions`). Scheduled jobs use `timeZone: "Asia/Kolkata"`.
- One Firebase project per environment — never add a `databaseId` parameter.
- Multi-doc writes use one `WriteBatch` or a transaction.
